{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>אֲשֶׁר נָשָׂאתִי אֶת יָדִי</b> — \"I raised it\": I raised it to swear by My throne. This is the language of Rashi. And R. Abraham [Ibn Ezra] said that it is figurative, like a person who raises his hand toward the heavens and swears, as in \"For I raise My hand to heaven\" (Deuteronomy 32:40), and \"He raised his right hand and his left hand toward heaven and swore\" (Daniel 12:7). And by way of truth, <b>נָשָׂאתִי אֶת יָדִי</b> — that I raised the arm of My might toward Myself, to give them the land. And likewise, \"For I raise My hand to heaven\" (ibid.) — that I raise the great Hand toward the heavens to be through it for eternal life. And \"He raised his right hand and his left hand toward heaven\" is not of this matter, for it is said of the angel clothed in linen who swore by the life of the world."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:33.508348093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}